course: dictionary
lesson: 9524
title: Words that sting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «A honeybee leaves its barbed stinger in the skin and dies after stinging.» Here a stinger is the sharp part an insect uses to sting, because the bee leaves it in the skin.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The box jellyfish has stinging cells on long tentacles, so tropical beaches put up stinger nets in summer.» Stinger nets keep stinging animals out of the water, so a stinger here can mean a stinging animal. The clues are the nets and the summer beaches.
explain: Some words carry a feeling too. When a stinger is a painful remark or ending, the writer means it hurts, like a bee sting. Use the same check as before: swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have more than one meaning, so check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: «Stinger» can mean the sharp part an insect uses to sting, such as a bee's stinger.
fact: «Stinger» can also mean an animal or plant that stings, such as a box jellyfish or a nettle.
fact: Informal use: a «stinger» is a painful hit, remark or ending that «stings».
exercise: «A honeybee leaves its barbed stinger in the skin and dies after stinging.» What is the stinger in this sentence? | The honey it makes | The bee's wings | The sharp part the bee uses to sting | *The flower it lands on
exercise: «The box jellyfish has stinging cells on long tentacles, so tropical beaches put up stinger nets in summer.» Why do beaches put up stinger nets? | To keep the sand from blowing away | *To keep stinging animals away from swimmers | To catch fish for dinner | To make the water warmer
exercise: «Stingless bees live in warm countries like Brazil, Mexico and Australia; their stingers are tiny and useless.» What is strange about their stingers? | They are very long and sharp | *They are tiny and useless for stinging | They glow in the dark | They are made of honey
test: «Stingless bees defend themselves by biting and crowding intruders.» How do stingless bees defend themselves? | By hiding in the honey | By flying away and never returning | *By biting and crowding intruders | By stinging with tiny stingers
test: «Most of these animals are shy and bite only when grabbed or stepped on.» When do most of these animals bite? | Only at night | Every time they see a person | Only in winter | *Only when grabbed or stepped on
exam: «Honeybees die after stinging people because the barbed stinger sticks in skin and tears out.» Why does a honeybee die after stinging a person? | Its honey runs out | It is stung by a wasp | *Its barbed stinger sticks in skin and tears out | It is too tired to fly away
